1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,600
Your cat isn't

2
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,300
knocking things off

3
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:01,680
the table

4
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:02,890
by accident.

5
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:03,980
That slow push

6
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:04,820
with one paw

7
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:06,000
is the same move

8
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,610
cats use on prey.

9
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:08,940
Tap it, and see

10
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:10,210
if it runs.

11
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,060
Then they watch

12
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,110
it fall.

13
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:13,180
Motion switches on

14
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:13,560
the hunter

15
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,850
in their brain.

16
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,060
But cat behaviorists

17
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:16,760
say there's

18
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,980
a second reason.

19
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:18,500
The first time

20
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,180
it happened,

21
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,400
you jumped up, shouted,

22
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,670
and came running.

23
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:22,900
Your cat noticed.

24
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,100
Now every glass

25
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:24,560
on the edge

26
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:24,860
is a way

27
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:25,800
to call you over.
